// PRACTICE PACK: the demo profile reads its practice items with it, and the craft simulator crafts with it in every profile.
//
// Real, and not checked in the game by SSE (verifiedDate is null): every family below, its side, affix names, tier
// numbers, modifier levels, ranges and wording; which families a crossbow can roll at all; the Siege Crossbow base
// (29-115 physical, 1.65 attacks per second; also 5% critical hit chance, reload time 0.75, Requires Level 79, 89 Str,
// 89 Dex, which this file does not need); and the tier each essence adds on a crossbow. All of it is Path of Exile 2
// patch 0.5.5 game data, item data (c) Grinding Gear Games, as Path of Building Community for PoE2 exports it
// (github.com/PathOfBuildingCommunity/PathOfBuilding-PoE2, MIT-licensed code; commit 49e9392, "Export 0.5.5 data",
// 10 Sep 2026: src/Data/ModItem.lua, src/Data/Bases/crossbow.lua, src/Data/Essence.lua). The comment over each
// family names the game's modifier group and the modifier ids of its tiers, Tier 1 first. Tier 1 is the best tier,
// counted among the tiers that item class can roll, as the game numbers them since 0.2.1 (docs/GAME.md, 1.5).
//
// Made up: every "weight" (Tier 1 250, Tier 2 500, every other tier 1000). The game files hold no weights, and the
// published community estimates may not be copied (docs/GAME.md, 4.1), so the craft simulator's odds are practice
// odds, not the game's. Nothing else in this file is made up.
//
// Left out: crossbows also roll "of Shelling" (Loads an additional bolt) and "of Bursting" (Loads 2 additional
// bolts); their two tiers are worded differently, which one family here cannot hold. For boots and helmets the pack
// has only the families the practice items need; their other stats are not in it.
